<title>SWEDEN: SCA posts 41 percent 9-mo profit drop.</title>
<headline>SCA posts 41 percent 9-mo profit drop.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forestry company SCA reports for the nine months ending September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 2,541  vs   4,312</p>
<p> Sales				     42,403  vs  50,275</p>
<p> EPS (SKR)				   7.62  vs   13.40</p>
<p> Operating costs			 36,517  vs  42,313</p>
<p> Operating surplus			5,886  vs   7,962</p>
<p> Depreciation			     2,613  vs   2,749</p>
<p> Associate interests			 11  vs     305</p>
<p> Operating profit			 3,284  vs   5,518</p>
<p> Net financial items	   CHARGE   743  vs   1,206   CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					    839  vs   1,393</p>
<p> Minorities				   199  vs     275</p>
<p> Net profit				 1,503  vs   2,644</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of company is Svenska Cellulosa Aktiebolaget SCA.</p>
<p>A Reuter poll of 15 analysts found SCA was expected to post a profit after financial items of 2.30 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
